const patch = "*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /private/tmp/entire-2157-pr-create.json
+{
+  "title": "fix(redact): preserve Grok encrypted reasoning payloads",
+  "head": "MuskanPaliwal:fix-grok-encrypted-content-2157",
+  "base": "main",
+  "draft": true,
+  "body": "Fixes #2157\n\n## The bug\n\nGrok Build stores a replay-critical reasoning attestation in `encrypted_content`. The value is opaque, high-entropy data that must remain byte-for-byte intact.\n\nEntire's JSONL redactor did not recognize this field as provider protocol data. The entropy scanner therefore replaced parts of the value with `REDACTED`, producing a transcript that Grok rejected when the session was restored.\n\n## The fix\n\nExclude the exact, case-sensitive `encrypted_content` key from JSONL scanning.\n\nThe boundary is deliberately narrow. It does not skip entire reasoning objects or match arbitrary encrypted-looking fields. Other fields in the same object remain subject to redaction.\n\nDirect field-classification coverage locks that exact allowlist entry in place, while the regression test exercises the real `JSONLContent` seam.\n\nThe regression test sends the same high-entropy value through `JSONLContent` twice:\n\n- `encrypted_content` must remain unchanged.\n- Ordinary `content` must still be redacted.\n\nThe sharded-redaction fixture now keeps its synthetic high-entropy value under `content`, so it continues exercising the entropy layer after `encrypted_content` becomes exempt.\n\nCodex also uses this key, but its agent-specific sanitizer removes Codex's non-portable ciphertext before storage. Focused sanitizer, checkpoint, and integration tests confirm that behavior remains intact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Reproduced the corruption with the focused regression test before the fix.\n- Confirmed the same regression test passes after the fix.\n- Ran focused Grok redaction and Codex sanitization tests.\n- Ran `mise run check`, including formatting, lint, race-enabled unit and integration tests, and deterministic E2E canaries.\n- Ran the final `mise run lint`: 0 issues.\n\nReal-agent E2E tests were not run."
+}
*** End Patch";
